Max change log (1998)
=====================

VERSION HISTORY
---------------
12/14/98 Max 2.26
	Rewrote connectivity tracing core algorithm:  
	sped up net selection and made it interruptable.

	Made selection undo optional (with default not to):
	sped up net selection and avoids thrashing
	due to unwieldly undo list.  Ffixes the problems
	where net selection got slower and slower as you
	repeated it!

	Tested internal hash code and augmented with autoresizing 
	and other embellishments to support label hashing (see below).
	Also eliminates potentially performance issues with
	groups, flylines and the max2 database consistency code.

	Added hashing on label text to speed up name based label
	searches (sped up net selection further).  Added duplicate
	label when ever labels are added.   Fixes "bug" where 64
	copies of labels were generated when reading certain
	problematic GDSII files.  

	Above fixes sped up VDD net selection on the "exu_job_mng"
	example (a 3MByte GDS-II file) from 21 seconds to 9 seconds
	(2.3 x).

	Fixed "coreleak" in coarse redisplay code that caused
	performance to bog down over time when working with large
	place and route blocks (for example).
	
	Fixed coares redisplay code to do more aggressive merging
	(speeds up redisplay particularly for place and route blocks,
	and reduces memory overhead for the coarse redisplay info
	(potentially an issue when dealing with large place and route
	blocks).

	Added "zoomed out" selection redisplay code that takes advantage
	of the coarse redisplay planes (speeds up selection redisplay).

	Above fixes sped up selection redisplay for the VDD net on
	the "exu_job_mg" example from >2 seconds to .2 seconds (10x).

	Removed flyline update overhead when no flylines present
	(speeds up GDS-II read in, for example).  

	Greatly reduced overhead for unmapped layers during GDS-II read
	in.
	
	Replaced standard IO with custom-IO primitives for GDS reading
	(speeds up GDS-II read in).

	Optimized GDS-II to not first write intermediate "CIF planes"
	when GDS-II layers mapped directly to Max layers (with out
	mask operations).  Sped up GDS-II read in and reduced memory
	requirement.

	Above changes sped up GDS-II read in on an example 12 Mbyte
	place and route block from 9 seconds to 6 seconds (1.5x).
	The ratio of RAM required to GDS_II file size was reduced
	from 4x to 3x.

	Added debug messages (controlled by GDS_READ_DEBUG tcl variable)
	to  give insight into some problematic GDS-II files. :-)
	
11/11/98 Max2.25
	Fixed performance bug in 'sel_what types' which was causing
	Max to get suggish when selection is large  and in some
	cases (in conjunction with bug below) to hang completely.
	
	Fixed periodic update scheduling, so user not completely shut out 
	when it bogs down.

	ZOT fixed for scmos etc. :-)

	Palette now shows selected types more obviously.

	Now restoring "selection" on edit pop
	(so user can immediately push back if desired). 

	Fixed edit_in_place push/pop bug.

	Fixed so labels containing brackets ('[',']') edit properly.

	Now correctly loads .tcl files for technology variants 
	(e.g. g25-mmc.tcl) 

	Modified so that variant technologys (eg g25-mmc) specified in
	the MAX_DEFAULT_TECH environment variable are used when files of
	the given technology are specified on the command line.

	Max now correctly handles (writes) instances whose id (instance name)
	is identical to the referenced def (cell name).

	Fixed memory management related bug.

	Fixed memory consistency checking code.

	Added "Import GDSII Setup..." to File menu.

	Added ability to scale input when reading GDSII.

	Added round off checking when reading GDSII.

	Added control of types of warnings generated when reading GDSII.

	Added "bbox <layer> <type>" statement for cifinput section of tech	
	files, to allow bboxes to be preserved when reading GDSII.
	(Still need to add to our tech files).

	Eliminated some per use processing after reading in
	GDSII (may speed up GDS reading of designs with large numbers
	of instances).

	Added "GDSII -> ASCII" to File menu.
	Improved readabily of ASCII translation of GDSII.
	
10/15/98 Max 2.24
	Added ability to write instance names as GDS propertys
	(give "iname propattr <num>" in cifoutput section of tech file)

	Removed 32 char restriction on gds string output 
	(to allow for long instance names ala those generated by the DPC)

	Removed grid DEBUG message.

10/13/98 Max 2.23
	flatten_cells fixed.

	Pat's Navigation window.

	Converted to fancy prop_menu's.

	View/Edit command (edit_push) fixed for cellnames with '$'

	Removed references to "Magic" in error messages. :-)

	Added "iname propattr <num>" option to cifinput section
	of tech file (to support instance name properties in GDS
	ala MMC.

	fixed megacell compiler initialization.

	Pat's NT changes integrated.
		
9/1/98  Max 2.22
	hacked extraction section to take noninteger lambda 
	and pass on to .ext files	

8/21/98 Max 2.21
	flexlm support (thanks to Pat!)
	removed restriction on design grids we can import. 
	Updated megacell compiler 
		LEE NOTE: menu_tool_cmd's not working since mc.tcl 
		sourced before max.tcl

8/19/98 Max 2.20
	Redisplay of Non-manhattan geometry (re)implemented
	Feedback redisplay bug fixed.
	Updated version of megacell compiler.
	
8/11/98 Max 2.19
	Labels now stay put on fixed layer (whether or not that layer is
	actually present at the location of the label).  This fixes a
	serious problem with netnames getting assigned to wrong nets that
	was causing trouble at Rendition, and may also have been interfering
	with netlist comparison on the MMC project.

	Label editing now works during subedit.

	By popular request, adding a label no longer requires two levels
	of dialog. :-)

	Tabing through entrys in label dialog no longer bogged down
	with all the little buttons in the compass rose etc.

	Fixed bug in coarse redisplay code that caused coredumps on reading 
	the same GDS file twice, reverting files etc.

8/7/98	Max 2.18
	Auto restart with new colormap fixed.
	Added auto disable of drc, labels, flylines, and iports on zoom out.
		disabled entrys are shown grey in palette.  Note that you can
		override by clicking on a disabled  entry.
	New fangled color_map/display_styles now installed for tsmc, g25 and g35.
		(note both versions work with all versions of Max so not critical)
	One off problem on box width fixed.
	Fixed redisplay bug when zoomed out so entire design is just a dot.

8/3/98  Max 2.17
	New spiffy redisplay finally done.
	fastd button in palette.
	Scroll bar pumps fixed.

7/14/98 Max 2.16

6/11/98 Max 2.15
	Uped max cif layers.

6/9/98  Max 2.14
	Contains support for RC extraction in MegaCells (ext_geometry ext_layers_parameters)

5/20/98 Max 2.13
	Fixs problem with single/pixel cell code that caused coredumps.
	Fixs coredumps due to buffer overflow on too many errors.
	CCT support updated.

5/7/98 Max 2.12

	Megacell compiler included in Max executable and under license
	control (capability "mc" needed to run Megacell Compiler)

	Fixed core dump when lay_grid called from tech/foo.tcl.
	Can now set default grid size for a technology in tech/foo.tcl, e.g.:
		set GRID(fine_default_size) .1
		set GRID(coarse_default_size) 1.0


5/5/98  Max 2.11
	Fixed drc bug that caused coredumps for Andrew.

	Added "Show All Labels" to view menu (controls
        whether comment labels are shown just for the edit cell or for all cells)

	Added support for cct2max

	Removed "Max2 Warning on startup"

4/21/98 Max 2.10
	More redisplay performance (added coarse paint planes)
	Fixed new flyline bug. :-)
	tech file now takes micron units in cifoutput and drc sections.
	now extracting typical wire width from m1 width.

4/9/98 Max 2.9
	More redisplay performance (1000x Max1 for 4x big-sram on mha's PC)
	Fixed flyline redisplay bug (during subedits).

4/1/98 Max 2.8
	Paint redisplay speeded up (5x Max1 for SRAM example on MMI SPARC's). 
	Full path of edit cell now given in window title.
	Added horizontal scrolling for list boxes.

3/19/98 Max 2.7
	Fixed bug that was causing Max2.6 to coredump under Solaris.

3/18/98 Max 2.6
	The "critical path" bug has been fixed.

	The "duplicate instance" bug has been fixed.

	Cleaned up redisplay and underlying graphics code in preparation for
	redisplay performance enhancements and possible NT port.

	Order of magnitude speed up on redisplay involving a large number
	of unexpanded instances (such as auto generated blocks at Rendition).
	(Redisplay now distinguishes between in close and zoomed out).

	Box that is too small to easily spot is now highlighted within a 
	cross-hair.

	Point label marks ('+') now are fixed size relative to layout, i.e.
	they do not stay same size on the display as you zoom out and hence
	clutter up the display.
 
2/27/98 Max 2.5
	rmed 0<n<63 restriction on GDS layers and types.
	now outputting correct last modified dates (vMain) on GDS output.
	Added "memory monitoring" code for tracking down memory consistency problems.
	Fixed background drc related intermittent coredump.
	Fixed cell selection related intermittent coredump.
	Fixed subedit/undo intermittent coredump.
	Fixed redisplay problem for subedits and changing expansion status in mulitlevel nested structures.
	Fixed redisplay problem with label text when hiding cell internals.
	
2/10/98 Max 2.4
	"Goto Coordinates" added
	"Flatten Cells" added
	brought drc back to life
	fixed extractor time stamp info.
	various bug fixes!
	FIRST COMPLETE Max2 VERSION!

1/20/98 Max 2.3
        Fixed db_cell_copy to copy polygons.
        Added rudimentary selection capability for polygons.
        Max manual updated to reflect switch from "spider" to "hand" cursor.

1/15/98 Max 2.2
	No known flakiness!
	DRC/Extractor still broken.	
	.max read/write still loses timestamps/bboxes.

